		TITLE	'Cortland Diagnostics Info';	This EdAsm/Asm816 source code file was converted to AsmIIGS;	by EdAsmCvtIIGS version 1.2d7 on 5/14/91 at 7:12:45 PM****************************************************************** This is the ROM Test Sequencer for Burn-IN & Self-Test** File Name: ROM.SEQ.              By Karl Grabe.  Cork.*** Documentation: TSKA 0047* Rev: Beta 2.0 14 Apr 86** Modification History:**       20-Jan-86: Created, KG*       17-Feb-86: Alpha 1.0, KG*       10-Mar-86: Alpha 2.0, KG.  Add Clock, Interrupt,Speed.*       24-Mar-86: Beta 1.0, KG. Add Interrupt, Staggered error status*       23-Apr-86: Beta 2.0, KG. Add NVR, Shadow, Ram Address*                                    Front Desk Bus   *                                    Port 1 status output*       08-Jan-87: Rom rev. 2.0 Alpha*               Fern Bachman*                  1. Added code to clear banks $E0 & $E1*                  2. Runs Burn-in diagsnostics continuously and writes*                     to NVR ram when SW0=low (0 volts)*                  3. Runs one cycle of burn in diags. when SW0=high*                     and will not write to NVR.*               Gus Andrade/Ray Montagne*                  1. Added sound diagnostics as test number $0C**                                       * Tests Available for Beta 2.0 and later revs**       Error No           Test*       ========           ================*       01                  ROM CHECKSUM*       02                  MOVING INVERSION RAM*       03                  SOFTSWITCH*       04                  RAM ADDRESS*       05                  FPI SPEED*       06                  SERIAL PORTS*       07                  REAL TIME CLOCK*       08                  BATTERY RAM*       09                  FRONT DESK BUS*       0A                  SHADOW*       0B                  INTERRUPTS*       0C                  SOUND TESTS**            Copyright Apple Computer Inc. 1986*                   All Rights Reserved****************************************************************;;****************************************************************** The Cortland Test Diagnostics operate in Burn-In and* Self Test modes:** IN BURN-IN:* The sequencer looks to Non Volatile Ram for a certain* sequence, put there by pre burn-in functional tester.* If this sequence is not found then the Pre-BI tester failed to set* up NVR or the UUT/NVR is bad so the test halts setting the FAIL.LED(D).* IF this sequence is correct then a tests mask (= what tests to run) in NVR* is used instead of the default mask. This allows the Pre-BI tester* to determine what tests are to be run in Burn-In.** The entire test sequence is repeated for a number of cycles and this number* is also programmable by the Pre-BI tester. When the cycle completes* the power off annunciator is activated to tell the BI controller that* the UUT is inactive and ready to power down. Test fail status ( if any )* is stored in NVR to be read by the Post-BI tester. The tester can thus* determine if a board failed in Burn-IN and if so what test failed,* it's error code, and during what cycle the last fail occurred.**...............................................................** For Self Test (User):* The test mask (ie what tests to run) for self test* is a subest of the Burn-IN test mask.** After all tests have been sucessfully completed a* continous 1 KHz frequence beep is emmitted.* A 'System Good' message is displayed on the screen.** If any tests fail then a 6 KHz beep is emmitted.* A 'System Bad: AABBCCDD' message is displayed.* where AA is the test number that failed and BB-DD is* the fail code. The fail code is output to port 1* at 1200 baud preceded by a '*'.** AN0/1 and disk port phases 1 & 2 are used to tell* the outside world that the test sequence is ongoing/complete and* and that the UUT has passed/failed the self test.** NVR is never read or written to by the sequencer.* Some of the tests may use NVR but if so they will restore* its contents after the test is complete.**...............................................................** External test software can use its own mask ( store in* C register ) by calling EXT.SEQ. The EXT.SEQ address is* stored just after the last test pointer in the Test* pointer table.* All 11 ( at present ) tests are represented by an on/off; bit in the C register when using the EXT.SEQ call.* The C LSB is the first test in the test table etc.*****************************************************************		EJECT;...............................................................;; Soft Switches for Burn In:;; Note: a) 'wr NVR' = write test STATUS (6) registers;           to Non Volatile Ram.;;       b) DIAGTYPE (MSB $C046) is active lo eg MSB=0 is a hi;          on the Burn In connector;; KG 04 Feb 86;________________________________________________________________;   |DIAGTYPE*|   SW0   |   SW1   |         MODE                |;================================================================;   |    0    |     0   |     0   |  Normal Power UP            |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    0    |     0   |     1   |  Control Panel              |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    0    |     1   |     0   |  Cold Restart               |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    0    |     1   |     1   |  Self Diagnostic, no wr NVR |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    1    |     0   |     X   |  BI Diagnostic 1, wr NVR    |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    1    |     1   |     X   |  Self Diagnostic, no wr NVR |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | BI.FLAG | BI.ALT  |  SELF   |  <-- Test s/w Equate Names  |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |  9/10   |   5/6   |  ----   |  <-- BI Connector pins      |;----------------------------------------------------------------;; Burn In Annunciator/Disk Port Truth Table:;; Note: The PASS/FAIL.LED (AN0 & Phase 1) signal also operates;       in self test. Use an LED connected via a buffer to game;       I/O connector/disk port to verify UUT without VDU.;;_______________________________________________________________;   |   AN0   |   AN1   |          MODE                         |;================================================================;   |    1    |    0    |  Passed last cycle, continue          |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    0    |    0    |  Failed last cycle, continue          |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    1    |    1    |  Pass, ready to power down            |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |    0    |    1    |  Fail, ready to power down            |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |PASS.LED |POWER.ON | <-- Equate Names to turn on  (1)      |;   |FAIL.LED |POWER.OFF| <-- Equate Names to turn off (0)      |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Phase 1 | Phase 2 | <-- Final System Test with cover on   |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | 13/14   |  17/18  | <-- BI Connector Pins                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;; Note: Cork uses disk port phase lines P1 & P2 to match AN0 & AN1;		EJECT;...............................................................;; Tests available:;; Note: Each TEST NO corresponds to a bit in the 16 bit;       C register on calling EXT.SEQ. If the bit is true;       then the test is run, else it is skipped.;       The test subroutine must clear the carry if the;       test passed, else set the carry. The sequencer;       automatically  passes a skipped test. Two different;       groups of tests can be run as defined in the equates file;       ( a third set can be defined in Battery backed up ram):;;_______________________________________________________________;   | TST NO  |  Test(s) performed                              |;================================================================;   | LSB: 0  |  Bank $FE/$FF Roms Checksum                     |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      1  |  Softswitch/STATEREG test                       |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      2  |  Ram:  Moving Inversions                        |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      3  |  Ram: Addressing                                |;---------------------------------------------------------------|;   |      4  |  FPI/Video Counters Speed verification          |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      5  |  Serial: Internal Loopback                      |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      6  |  Real Time Clock                                |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      7  |  Battery Ram                                    |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |      8  |  Front Desk Bus Processor & Rom                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     09  |  Shadow register                                |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     10  |  Interrupts                                     |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     11  |  Sound                                          |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     12  |  -                                              |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     13  |  -                                              |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |     14  |  -                                              |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | MSB:15  |  -                                              |;----------------------------------------------------------------		EJECT***************************************************************; Error Message: "System Bad: AABBCCDD; Where AA is the test number that failed.;;_______________________________________________________________;   | Test     | Fail Codes                                     |;================================================================;   | ROM     |  BBCC= Failed Checksum, DD=01->Ram err          |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Ram 1   |  BB=BANK, CC=ADDRESS                            |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Speed   |  BB=1:Stuck slow, BB=2: Stuck fast. CC=Bad Value|;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Soft.sw |  BB=STATEREG BIT, CC=READ SOFTSWITCH ADDRESS    |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Ram MOVI|  BB=BANK, CC=BIT                                |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | Ser.tst |  See Test code                                  |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | IRQ     |  See Test code                                  |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | CLOCK   | If DD=01-> Tool Error encountered, BB= error #  |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | FDB     | BBCC= Failed Checksum, DD=01-> Tool error       |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | RAM addr| As Moviram                                      |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | BAT.RAM | BB=1-> Address test, CC=Failed Address          |;   |         | BB=2-> Pattern, CC=Pattern, DD= Address         |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   | SHADOW  | None                                            |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |         |                                                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |         |                                                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |         |                                                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;   |         |                                                 |;----------------------------------------------------------------;****************************************************************** Note:  For debugging the sequencer code Use SEQ.DEBUG =1*        This swaps DIAGTYPE for SW2. Note that SW2 for*        debugging is inverted to DIAGTYPE ie a 0 is*        required to be in Burn In. Also do a JMP $FF7140*        to get into the diagnostics code. SEQ.DEBUG is a*        variable at the beginning of file ROM.SEQ and is used*        for conditional assembly.*****************************************************************		TITLE	'65SC816 word size macros'*********************************************************** 65816 Macros for word size switching** kg Sep 85*************************************************************************************************		MACRO		NTV		; 		CLC		XCE		;t into native mode		ENDM**		MACRO		NTV16		; GET		CLC		XCE		;ET E = 0 ( Native mode )		REP	#%00110000		LONGA	ON		LONGI	ON		ENDM**		MACRO		EML		; SET		SEC		XCE		;ET E=1 ( Emulation mode )		LONGA	OFF		LONGI	OFF		ENDM;******************************************		MACRO		DATA16		; SET		REP	#%00110000	;SET M=0, X=0 (16 BIT)		LONGA	ON		LONGI	ON		ENDM**		MACRO		DATA8		; 		SEP	#%00110000	;SET M=1, X=1 (8 BIT )		LONGA	OFF		LONGI	OFF		ENDM;******************************************		MACRO		IND16		; 		REP	#%00010000	;X=0 ( 16 bit index )		LONGI	ON		ENDM**		MACRO		MEM16		; 		REP	#%00100000	;M=0 (16 bit memory)		LONGA	ON		ENDM**;****************************************		MACRO		IND8		; 		SEP	#%00010000	;Set X=1 ( 8bit index )		LONGI	OFF		ENDM**		MACRO		MEM8		; 		SEP	#%00100000	;Set M=1 ( 8 bit memory )		LONGA	OFF		ENDM;****************************************** FPI FAST/SLOW macros.*		MACRO		SLOW		; 		STZ	CYAREG	;Go into slow mode		ENDM		MACRO		FAST		; 		LDA	#%10000000		STA	CYAREG	;Set fpi fast		ENDM;****************************************** Message length macro* Uses same format as ProDOS pathname length** Use:*      MSG.0 MSG.LEN*           ASC "<Fist message 0>"*      MSG.1 ASC "The 2nd message"*      .*      .*      MSG.n DFB $00  ;Last message*;****************************************		MACRO		MSG_LEN		; 		DC.B	MSG_&SYSINDEX-*-1		ENDM			TITLE	'DIAGNOSTIC HARDWARE EQUATES'****************************************************************** Hardware equates:** (Game I/O) & B/I pad Signals:* Note: We in Cork use Disk phase signals for* Final System Test pass/fail & test ongoing/complete* status. Singapore will use AN0 & AN1 instead.** By Karl Grabe. Apple Computer Inc.*****************************************************************	; SEG	$00PASS_LED		EQU	SETAN0	;Turn on pass LEDPASS_LEDD		EQU	$C0E3	;Phase 1 on disk port hi (for CORK FST)FAIL_LED		EQU	CLRAN0	;Turn off pass LEDFAIL_LEDD		EQU	$C0E2	;Phase 1 on disk port loPOWER_ON		EQU	CLRAN1	;Turn on power cycle LED (Test in progress)POWER_OND		EQU	$C0E4	;Phase 2 disk port hi (Test in progress)POWER_OFF		EQU	SETAN1	;Turn off power cycle LED (Ok to power off: tst fin)POWER_OFFD	EQU	$C0E5	;Phase 2 lo (test finished)BI_FLAG		EQU	BUTN2	;True: UUT is in Burn-In (For debuggin,Norm use DIAGTYPE)SELF		EQU	BUTN0	;True: we are in self/user diagnostic (NO wr to NVR)NVR_FREE		EQU	$0361	;Start of free battery ram spaceDIAG_VARS		RECORD	0	;Diagnostic vars** ZP variables:*		ORG	$10BAT_RAM_PTR	DS.B	4	;Used by READ.NVR routine		ORG	$F9ZP_PNTR		DS.B	2	;Zero page pointerTST_PTR		DS.B	2	;Points to testCHK_BEG		DS.B	2	;Start address to checksum** Non ZP variables:*		ORG	$300NVR_BEG		EQU	*	;Non vol ram image starts hereBI_STATUS		DS.B	4	;Test Results -- Currently use only 4 bytesBI_FAILMASK	DS.B	2	;BI.STATUS was 6-byte, becomes 'OR'ed of all failed testsBI_COUNTER	DS.B	2	;Counts the number of cycles doneBI_PASSES		DS.B	2	;Number of passes in BI (=Board level Burn-In)BI_FIRSTF		DS.B	2	;SEQ.COUNTER value at first failBI_LASTF		DS.B	2	;SEQ.COUNTER value at last failCYCLES_MAX	DS.B	2	;Number if test cycles to run in BI (Programmable)VALID_CHK		DS.B	3	;3 byte signature to validate next bytes BI.ALT.MASKBI_ALT_MASK	DS.B	2	;The PreBI tester can program what tests to run in BINVR_END		EQU	*	;Non vol ram image ends hereTST_STATUS	DS.B	6	;Temp storage of fail status in BIERRCODE1		EQU	TST_STATUS+1ERRCODE2		EQU	TST_STATUS+2BI_FAIL		DS.B	2	;True if any test fails during BI sequence (1 byte)ST_FAIL		DS.B	2	;True if a test fails in self testTST_MASK		DS.B	2	;Two byte test mask - what tests to runCYCLE_COUNT	DS.B	2	;One byte BI cycle counter: init with CYCLES.MAXTST_COUNT		DS.B	2	;Test counter for sequencer (use only one byte)NO_TESTS		DS.B	2	;Initial value of TST.COUNT, ie total no of testsCUR		DS.B	2	;"Curser" for ROM.COUT ( use one byte only )PORT_ON		DS.B	2	;True for ROM.COUT to print to Port 1KEY_VERSION	DS.B	2	;Key micro version number (1 byte);; For Battery ram tests:;		ORG	$0800	;Disk s/w must avoid this areaBRAM_TEMP		DS.B	256	;Used to hold contents during testsBRAM_WORK		DS.B	256	;Working Bram areaBRAM_WORK1	DS.B	256	;Working Bram area 2;; FDB rom checksum:;POINTER		DS.B	2	;What FDB up byte ram/rom to readRESULT		DS.B	2	;Where tool leaves rom/ram byte readFDB_BUF		DS.B	4096	;Read FDB rom code in here NB: 4k Buffer		ENDR;; Tool vars in bank $E1  (Must be cleared to zero); See FDB tool source code on following:;; Serial PORT1.COUT routine:;SLOT		EQU	1	;Port 1 is in slot 1SLOT_ADDR		EQU	SLOT*16*16+$C000INIT_OFF		EQU	SLOT_ADDR+$D	;Pascal 1.1 init pointer offsetWRITE_OFF		EQU	SLOT_ADDR+$F	;Pascal 1.1 write pointer offsetINIT_JMP		EQU	$10	;10-12  ;WRITE_JMP		EQU	$12	;12-13  ;Zero page locations usedSER_ZBANK		EQU	$2000	;Where slot 1 IO rom is called from in zero bank;; Moving Inversions Ram;LOC		EQU	$04RAMBANK		EQU	$F0RAMENDADDR	EQU	$F2RAMBEGADDR	EQU	$F4THEDATA		EQU	$07MOD~		EQU	$09FLIP		EQU	$0B;; Serial Test Equates;SCCCMD		EQU	$BFFDSCCDATA		EQU	$BFFFCHAINDEX		EQU	$3CCHBINDEX		EQU	$3BCNT1		EQU	$0800CNT2		EQU	$0801CNT3		EQU	$0802CNT4		EQU	$0803STCNT1		EQU	$0804STCNT2		EQU	$0805STCNT3		EQU	$0806STCNT4		EQU	$0807SERIRQCNT		EQU	$0809CHHSK		EQU	$080ACHDTR		EQU	$080BDATA		EQU	$080CREGNO		EQU	$080DSERMASK		EQU	$080EMASKDATA		EQU	$080FSERIRQTEMP1	EQU	$0810SERIRQTEMP2	EQU	$0811SERIRQTEMP3	EQU	$0812ZER1		EQU	$BEZER2		EQU	$E2LIMIT		EQU	$FF	;??????;...............................................................; FDB.EQU; Front Desk Bus Test Equates; KG;...............................................................	; SEG	RUNBANKFDB_ROM_GYRO_A	EQU	$1000	;Start of rom address in GyroFDB_ROM_B		EQU	$1400	;Start of rom address in GSFDB_ROM_E		EQU	$1FFF	;End; FDB rom checksums:FDB_REV1		EQU	$3DE6	;No longer supported kg/apr/86FDB_REV2		EQU	$F772FDB_REV3		EQU	$2672	;Checksum for all new rom releases;;FDB Tool table for RDMEM;RD_KEY_DATA	EQU	10*4+$8000FDB_TOOL_ADDR	EQU	11*4+$8000NOT_SW		EQU	$FF	;Flags non standard soft switchFAST_LIM		EQU	$191A	;Lower and upper fast speed limits, ER 1SLOW_LIM		EQU	$0C0D	;Lwr and upr slow speed limits for ROM, ER 2	; SEG	$00	;Code was written for bank $00CUSIRQCNT		EQU	$7000CUSIRQSTS		EQU	$7002CUSLINENO		EQU	$7004CUSIRQSRCE	EQU	$7006IRQTEMP1		EQU	$7008IRQTEMP2		EQU	$700AIRQTEMP3		EQU	$700CSHADPATT1		EQU	$5A5ASHADPATT2		EQU	$A5A5SHDLENGHT		EQU	$0400SHDSTRT		EQU	$000A	;Must be 4 bytes in Pg 0SHDBIT		EQU	$000ESHDDATA		EQU	$0800XTEMP		EQU	10*		TITLE	'Doc diags. equate file';********************************************************** Doc.equ: This file contains all the equates required by the*          rom based Ensoniq DOC diagnostics.*;********************************************************;;SGCONTROL		EQU	$C03C	; Sound Glu control registerSGDATA		EQU	$C03D	; Sound Glu data registerSGADDRL		EQU	$C03E	; Sound Glu address reg lowSGADDRH		EQU	$C03F	; Sound Glu address reg high;;;;       Sound Glu control register bit definition;;          +---+---+---+---+---+---+---+---+;          | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |;          +---+---+---+---+---+---+---+---+;            |   |   |   | |_______________|;            |   |   |   |         |;            |   |   |   |         +---------- System volume setting;            |   |   |   +-------------------- RESERVED;            |   |   +------------------------ Addr. 0=hold, 1=incr;            |   +---------------------------- Dev sel. 0=DOC, 1=Ram;            +-------------------------------- Busy bit: 1=busy 0=free;DOC_NO_INC	EQU	$04	; select the Doc no auto incr vol = $04DOC_INCR		EQU	$24	; Doc, auto inc. sys vol = 04 RAM_INCR		EQU	$64	; ram, auto inc. sys vol =$04;;;**********************************************************                 Misc equates*;********************************************************;;IRQ_VECTOR	EQU	$E10010	; Master interrupt vector;;;**********************************************************                 Doc register names*;********************************************************;;DOC_FREQL		EQU	$00	; frequency low registerDOC_FREQH		EQU	$20	;DOC_VOLUME	EQU	$40	;DOC_WAVE_DATA	EQU	$60	;DOC_WAVE_PTR	EQU	$80	; doc waveform table pointerDOC_CONTROL	EQU	$A0	; doc control registerDOC_BANK_RES	EQU	$C0	; bank, table size, res.DOC_IRQ_REG	EQU	$E0	; osc. interrupt registerDOC_OSC_ENB	EQU	$E1	; oscillator enable registerDOC_AD_CONV	EQU	$E2	; oscillator analog to digital converter;;;;********************************************************** Doc.data.equ: This module contains the ram work area equates*               for the rom doc diagnostics.*;********************************************************;;;DOC_DATA_EQU	EQU	0	;IRQ_COUNTER	EQU	0	;FAIL_TIMER	EQU	2	; fail safe timerCYCLE_COUNTER	EQU	4	;OSC_BUSY		EQU	6	; oscillator busy flagTESTDATA		EQU	8	; temp variable for data pattern;;